  ('Team pairs quarter finals', 'team-pairs-quarter-finals', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'A great 4-1 win at Mevagissey B saw Tregonissey A jump up to 3rd in the Victory League.', 'St Neot breezed into the semi finals of the Team pairs beating Bugle B by 3 straight frames with Darren Lock and Ant Maddams winning both there games and Darren Oshea and Steve Courts the other', 'Bethel A got a great 3 nil win at Pelynt to progress', 'St Blazey A also advanced after getting the first 3 frames at Bethel D. Liam Reynolds and Chris Brown saw off Geoff Hawken and Paul Baron in the opener by 12 points and Stuart Dewings knocked in a 30 break straight away partnering Billy Vigus to help them beat Jason Pascoe and Steve Benallack by 53 points and they then won a respotted Black ball frame against Geoff and Paul to seal the well deserved win.

Bethel A got a great 3 nil win at Pelynt to progress Andy Peers and Garry Stephens beat Richard Broad and Len Flower by 10 points in the opener and Matt Green and Mark Ashton got 2 big wins in the next 2 frames to seal the win.

Tregonissey A beat there C team by 3 frames to nil to also advanced into the semi finals with the draw being done this week.

In a delayed Team handicap plate game Mevagissey B overcame Gorran Haven by 3 frames to 1 Warren Ball beat Pete Chambers on the Black to put Gorran ahead but wins for Ben Rothwell Matt Rowe and Nathan Shaw sets up a home semi final against Bugle B for the meva boys on the 18th February.

Also a delayed Team handicap game Mevagissey C beat Tregonissey C by 3 frames to 1 Kelly McMullen beat Glyn Tamblin for treggys frame with Ben Baker Rich Tamblin and Mark Ferguson all winning to set up a home semi final against Bugle A.', '2025-02-05', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('St Blazey A get much needed win', 'st-blazey-a-get-much-needed-win', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'A great 4-1 win at Mevagissey B saw Tregonissey A jump up to 3rd in the Victory League.', 'St Blazey A got a great much needed win at Tregonissey A to help there efforts to get away from the relegation places.', 'Bethel A moved into joint 3rd place after beating Pelynt by 4 frames to 1', 'After going 2 frames down with Ryan Bilson and Jason Cocks winning for the home side Stuart Dewings Liam Reynolds and stand in Gavin Dyche recorded wins to see them edge closer to the pack above.

Leaders Bugle A suffered a defeat at home by the odd frame to St Neot Jake Moore and Gary Spencer got wins but the away side prevailed through Steve Courts, Chris Perring and Darren Lock.

Bethel A moved into joint 3rd place after beating Pelynt by 4 frames to 1. Bob Stephens took out Richard Broad in the opener but Len Flower levelled things up beating Andy Peers but Matt Green Mark Ashton and Garry Stephens all won to seal a good win.

Leaders of the Rees league Mevagissey A picked up the runabout shield after beating Bethel C by the odd frame. Matt Chesterfield and Ben Prynn put them 2 frames ahead but Roger Smithson beat Darren Powell pull one back but Rich Lakemans black ball win over Howard Brett was crucial to seal the win as Paul Smithson beat Rob Blamey in the final frame.

Lerryn picked up a great 3-2 win at St Blazey B with Graham Hoskin Terry Middleton and James Stephens all winning.

Bethel B took 4 frames at Mevagissey C as Matt Moore Craig Nicholls Ady Dyche and Darren Biggen all successful with Mark Ferguson winning on the Black to get the home point.

