  ('Team handicap week', 'team-handicap-week-2', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bethel A got a great 3 nil win at Pelynt to progress.', 'Tregonissey A advanced to the team handicap final after a good 3-1 home win against Mevagissey A', 'Bethel A got a great 3 nil win at Pelynt to progress', 'They took a 2 frame lead as Kevin Harris beat James Tomlinson and Geoff Merriman took out Rich Lakeman but Matt Chesterfield made 2 x 32 breaks as he thrashed John Bates to pull a frame back but Jason Cocks beat Ben Prynn in a close next game to seal the win.

In the final They will play Bugle A who went to Mevagissey C and got the first 3 frames with Josh Bristow. Gary Spencer who knocked in a 33 break and Andrew Best the successful cueman.

In the Plate competition holders Mevagissey B have made the final again after a really close win over Bugle B they started well with Nathan Shaw getting the better of Dave Rundle but Keith Moore ''s black ball win against Dave Kendall levelled things to with Matt Rowe putting them ahead again beating Mark Sturtridge only for Mike Williams winning a very low scoring game against Ben Prynn leaving Mark Gregory''s pink ball win in the last frame settling the evening.

Steve Benallack got Bethel A off to a good start against St Blazey B beating Nick Ferguson and Geoff Hawken doubled there lead after a long drawn out frame taking the pink and black to pip Martin Richards and victory was secured with Paul Baron beating Gavin Dyche to set up a repeat of last year''s final.', '2025-02-20', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bethel A gain ground on the Victory leaders', 'bethel-a-gain-ground-on-the-victory-leaders', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Victory League leaders Bugle A suffered a 3 2 defeat at home to Mevagissey B.', 'Victory League leaders Bugle A suffered a 3-2 defeat at home to Mevagissey B meaning Bethel A closed the gap at the top of the league to 6 points after beating Tregonissey B 5-0 and they have a game in hand.', 'Darren Lock knocked in a 48 break against John Daniell', 'Gary Spencer (35 break) and Josh Bristow got there wins against the Meva boys with Nathan Shaw, Matt Rowe and Dave Kendall victorious for the visitors.

Bethel A had comfortable wins against bottom of the table Tregonissey B with Garry Stephens having a 35 break as he beat Darren Roberts.

Darren Lock knocked in a 48 break against John Daniell giving St Neot a winning start against Pelynt. Andrew Gooch levelled things up but Mark Story put the away side ahead again but Jamie Daniell and Rich Broad won for the home side to seal the win.

Bethel D got a much needed win at St Blazey A by the odd frame with 4 tight frames on the night with wins for Geoff Hawken, Jason Pascoe and a great win for Steve Benallack over Liam Reynolds in the final frame.

Bugle B inflicted the 1st defeat of the season to Mevagissey A and also got there hands on the runabout shield they went into a 3-0 lead through Dave and Colin Rundle and Keith Moore with Matt Chesterfield and Ben Prynn pulling back the last 2 frames for the hosts.

St Blazey B lost the first 3 frames at Gorran Haven but managed to take the final 2 and now only sit 2 points ahead of Bugle B who have a game in hand.

Tregonissey C took the 1st 2 frames at home to Bethel B through Predator Tregale and Jowan Truman but the away side hit back to win as Craig and Terry Nicholls along with Darren Biggen all won.

Les Shakespeare and Graham Hoskin grabbed the final 2 frames for Lerryn at Bethel C after Ben Stunell Howard Brett and Roger Smithson all won for the hosts.

