  ('Tight race to the finish in the victory league', 'tight-race-to-the-finish-in-the-victory-league', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Victory League leaders Bugle A suffered a 3 2 defeat at home to Mevagissey B.', 'Bethel A won 4 1 at St Neot to close the gap to 2 points on leaders Bugle A going into last nights clash between the sides.', 'Bugle B boosted there chances of finishing runners up as they moved into 2nd place', 'Garry Stephens great win against Darren Lock along with wins for Matt Green Mark Ashton and Andy Peers saw them get the win with only 2 games left in the season.

At the other end of the league Tregonissey B are relegated despite beating St Blazey A by 3 frames to 2 with the Blazey boys needing 2 big wins in there remaining games to stand any chance of staying up.

Mevagissey B remain 3rd coming from 2 down to beat Pelynt and Tregonissey A picked up 4 points at Bethel D who''s only winner was Paul Baron.

Mevagissey A only need 1point from there remaining 2 games to be crowned Rees league champions after taking all 5 frames against there C team.

Bugle B boosted there chances of finishing runners up as they moved into 2nd place after beating Bethel C by the odd frame putting them a point ahead of St Blazey B with both teams having 2 games left with Keith Moore and Colin and Dave Rundle there winners with Roger Smithson and Howard Brett getting the away points.

Lerryns final home game of the season saw them beat Tregonissey C by the odd frame as John Hancock, Terry Middleton and David Vipond all won with Darren Elliott and Mark Richards replying.

Rob Bunney got Gorran Haven off to good start at Bethel B beating Matt Moore but that proved there only success as Ady Dyche, Mike Haley and Craig and Terry Nicholls all won for the home side.

