  ('Almost there', 'almost-there-2', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bugle A need 1 point from there final game to be champs of the Victory league', 'Bugle A need 1 point from there final game to be champs of the Victory league', 'There is going to be a nervous night in the Rees league on Tuesday', 'After hammering nearest rivals Bethel A 4-1 with Justin Oxenham knocking in a 31 break when beating Mark Ashton with Garry Stephens sneaking past Josh Bristow for the visitors point.

St Blazey A are relegated after losing all 5 frames at home to St Neot and join Tregonissey B who were already down and suffered a 4 1 defeat at Bethel D in a match which was far closer than the scoreline suggests.

Tregonissey A regained 3rd place rushing into a 3 nil lead against visitors Pelynt with Geoff Merriman Kevin Harris and Ryan Bilson all winning but Jamie Daniell and Len Flower pulled back the last 2 frames for the away side.

Mevagissey A are Rees league champions after beating Gorran Haven by the odd frame with wins for Matt Chesterfield Darren Powell and Ben Prynn who remains unbeaten for the season with Warren Ball and Lee McKinstry winning for the home side.

There is going to be a nervous night in the Rees league on Tuesday as St Blazey B beat Mevagissey C by 5 frames to nil to jump ahead of Bugle B by a single point after they beat Tregonissey C by the odd frame. Clive Stuthridge had a 30 break in defeating Mark Ferguson won which he needed but fairly ease wins for George Taylor, Martin Richards, Kyle Masters and Gavin Dyche got the whitewash.

Darren Elliott and Dave Tregale in got Treggys point against Bugle B who replied through Keith Moore and Colin and Dave Rundle Bethel B got 4 points at home to Lerryn to move up 2 places in the league with Craig Nicholls edging out Graham Hoskin in the last frame to seal the result.

