  ('Bugle A and Mevagissey A seal titles', 'bugle-a-and-mevagissey-a-seal-titles', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bugle A are Victory League champions despite a defeat at relegated Tregonissey B', 'Bugle A are Victory League champions despite a defeat at relegated Tregonissey B as Gary Spencer won the 2nd frame of the night to confirm them as worthy winners with Andrew Best also victorious Mark Haworth Darren Roberts and Kyle Bennetts won for the home side.', 'St Blazey B and Bugle B are playing a playoff at Mevagissey on Monday 31st March after both finishing on 51 points', 'Bethel A went break crazy as they sealed the runners up spot beating nearest rivals Tregonissey A 4-1 Andy Peers 36 Garry Stephens 36 and Mark Ashton 33 all won along with Matt Green with Jason Cocks taking the away point.

Darren Lock, Steve Courts and Darren Oshea got wins for St Neot at home to Mevagissey B who replied through Dave Kendall and Mark Gregory and Pelynt edged out St Blazey A by the odd frame with Mark Cockayne and Liam Reynolds who knocked in a 33 break winners as they prepare for life in the Rees league next season.

St Blazey B and Bugle B are playing a playoff at Mevagissey on Monday 31st March after both finishing on 51 points.

The Blazey boys dropped 2 frames to Craig Nicholls and Ady Dyche of Bethel B meaning Bugle''s 4-1 win at home to Mevagissey C was enough to get the playoff with Roy Bayliss having a 34 break and Colin Rundle taking a long winded very close final frame against Glyn Tamblin to seal the result.

Mevagissey A captain Ben Prynn was unbeaten all season in the league and beat Predator Tregale this week as his team beat Tregonissey C by 4 frames to 1 with Amanda Fleming beating Rob Blamey for the visitors.

Dan Pascoe beat Leigh Rosevear last up to help Gorran Haven beat Bethel C by the odd frame earlier wins for Warren Ball and Lee McKinstry were cancelled out by Howard Brett and James Smithson.

