  ('Annual General Meeting 2025 (AGM)', 'annual-general-meeting-2025-agm', 'League Meetings', '[]'::jsonb, 'St Blazey and District snooker league AGM was held at Bethel social club on Tuesday 8th July 2025', 'St Blazey and District snooker league AGM was held at Bethel social club on Tuesday 8th July 2025', null, 'Present: Chris Perring president Garry Stephens chairman Geoff Hawken secretary Keith Moore vice chairman Matt Green, Clive Stuthridge, Ryan Orchard, Justin Oxenham, Gary Spencer, Mark Cockayne (all committee) Jason Pascoe, Andrew Best, Terry Nicholls, Craig Nicholls, John Daniell, Adrian Evans, Gavin Dyche. Apologies: Richard Pearson, Darren Biggen, Mark Gregory, Lee McInstry.

Introduction

Chairman opened the meeting and thanked everyone for their attendance. Minutes of the 2023/24 season were read and agreed as a true record.

1. Victory league beat liskeard league 8 6 at st neot
2. Rees league beat liskeard league 1 by 9 6 at st blazey
3. On line banking for league comps etc is working well
4. The runabout shield was found late in the season and was passed on to the current holders but teams must display the shield when in possession of the shield
5. Runabout shields will start at bethel a and bugle b
6. Secretary thanked everyone for there support during the season especially john daniell mark cockayne and all the people who prepared tables reffing and making venues available with adrian evans doing a fantastic job at mevagissey which hosted several finals
7. Boynton trophy buy/sponsor a player would not be displayed before everyone has paid there £5 as 3 people never paid there money last time
8. Secretary thanked everyone for there help over the last season john daniell for doing the fixtures mark cockayne who has been amazingly good on the website
9. Thanks to steve courts and gavin dyche for preparing the st blazey v liskeard and rees league v liskeard 1st division games
10. Putting the presentation night back by a couple of weeks certainly helped especially with 2 new games/finals to be played

1. Secretary reported a £764.48 surplus on the season
2. Competition entries were up by £111
3. Trophies and engraving was £215.24 down on the season
4. There were no website charges last season
5. Altogether a very good your financially
6. Mark cockayne proposed to accept the accounts
7. Matt green seconded passed unanimously
8. Election of officer''s and committee
9. Passed onblock

1. Bugle a have moved to luxulyan to play
2. Secretary asked for the extra player to be named on the scprecard when put on facebook helping him when he does the report for the st austell voice
3. Secretary would distribute fixtures and handicaps to all the clubs when they are available
4. Where 2 tables are used for league games nominated table 1 would have frames 1 3 and 5 played on them and table 2 would have frames 2 and 4 played on them

There being no further business the chairman closed the meeting at 20.10hrs', '2025-07-24', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('2025-2026 Snooker Leagues up and running', '20245-2026-snooker-leagues-up-and-running', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'The st blazey and district snooker league got up and running with all 3 games in the victory league ending 3-2', 'The St Blazey and District Snooker League got up and running with all 3 games in the victory league ending 3-2', 'New look Luxulyan (formally Bugle A) suffered defeat at Tregonissey A by the odd frame', 'Nathan Shaw got Mevagissey B off to a good start beating Mark Ashton of Bethel A. With Matt Green levelling things up getting past Dave Kendall then Garry Stephens knocked in a 38 break against Ben Rothwell to put bethel ahead again but Matty Rowe powered past Andy Peers for parity but Paul Baron had a fine 35 break in the decider to clinch the win with Nathan Shaw playing his second game of the night.

Liam Jones won a respotted black ball frame against Matt Mills to get Bethel D off to a good start at promoted Mevagissey A but Ben Prynn played well to beat Bob Stephens to even up, then Jason Pascoe took out Matt Chesterfield to put the visitors ahead again with Geoff Hawken coming from a long way back to beat Darren Powell to seal the win with matt mills beating Steve Benallack in his second game of the night.

New look Luxulyan (formally Bugle A) suffered defeat at Tregonissey A by the odd frame as Jason Cocks, Kev Harris and Geoff Merriman won for the home side with Harrison Burdon and Andrew Best replying.

Last years wooden spoonists Tregonissey C got off to a flyer beating Lerryn 4-1 with wins for Amanda Fleming, Darren Elliott, Mark Richards and predator Tregale with Les Shakespeare replying.

Tregonissey B went to Bugle and picked up the runabout shield with a 4-1 win with James Holmes, Darren, Mark Haworth and Jowan Truman on target with dave rundle winning for the home side.

Mevagissey C went 3 up at Bethel C as Rich Tamblin, Adrian Evans and Mark Ferguson all won with Ben Stunell and Roger Smithson pulling the last 2 frames back for the home side.

Gorran Haven started with a home win as they took out Bethel B by the odd frame.

