  ('Big result for Luxulyan', 'big-result-for-luxulyan', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'St Blazey A must be favourites for the Rees league after beating  Tregonissey B by 4 frames to 1', 'With there rivals all dropping points luxulyan took full advantage taking all 5 frames at Mevagissey B to go 3 points clear at the top of the Victory league in what is looking to be a very tight battle to win the league this year.', 'St Blazey A must be favourites for the Rees league after beating Tregonissey B by 4 frames to 1', 'Tregonissey A were 2 down at Bethel D after Jason Pascoe and Geoff Hawken won for the home side but Jason Cocks Mark Paulson and Andrew Gooch all won to grab the win to stay 2nd.

Bethel A also dropped 2 frames at St Blazey B with Clive Stuthridge and Gavin Dyche winning for the home side with Mark Ashton Garry Stephens and Paul Baron replying.

Mevagissey A picked up a great win at Pelynt through Ben Prynn Darren Powell and Matt Mills with Phil Ormond and Jamie Daniell replying.

St Blazey A must be favourites for the Rees league after beating Tregonissey B by 4 frames to 1 and taking the runabout shield as Ryan Orchard took out Stuart Dewings for the solitary home point with Mark Cockayne getting a 30 break in his win.

Gorran Haven remain second despite a 3 2 defeat at Bugle as Colin and Dave Rundle along with Jake Moore won for the home side with Rob Bunney and Matt Fox replying.

Tregonissey C are having a much improved season and moved up to joint 3rd in the league after beating Bethel B they went 3 up after wins for Amanda Fleming Predator Tregale and Mark Richards with Darren Biggen and Craig Nicholls pulling back the final 2 frames for the home side.

Mevagissey C are also joint 3rd after beating Lerryn by the odd frame as Rich Tamblin Mark Ferguson and Oliver Watson all won with James Stephens and Les Shakespeare getting the visitors points.

