  ('Bethel A hit the top', 'bethel-a-hit-the-top-of-the-victory-league', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bugle have moved up to 2nd after a great 4  1 win at struggling Bethel C.', 'Bethel A have hit the top of the Victory league after a comprehensive 5 nil win at home to Pelynt to be 2 points clear There were big wins for Garry Stephens Paul Baron Matt Green Andy Peers and Mark Ashton.', 'Bugle have moved up to 2nd after a great 4 1 win at struggling Bethel C.', 'Matt Chesterfield and Kyle Bennetts put Mevagissey A 2 up against there B team but that was as good as it got as Dave Kendalls single point win over Matt Mills and victories for Mark Gregory and Nathan Shaw saw there rivals take the bragging rights.

Tregonissey A remain unbeaten after beating St Blazey B with 2 black ball wins for Kevin Harris against Gavin Dyche and Andrew Gooch beating George Taylor in the nights final frame Jason Cocks also won with Clive Stuthridge and Ian Millward getting the away points.

Steve Benallack and Geoff Hawken got Bethel D a useful 2 points at St Neot as they try to pull away from the bottom of the league Darren Lock Steve Courts and Chris Perring took the home frames.

St Blazey B are already 8 points clear in the Rees league after whipping Bethel B leaving them pointless although 3 frames were very close on the night.

Lerryn picked up a cracking 4 1 win at home to Tregonissey B joining 3 other sides on 13 points Ryan Orchard took the away frame as James Stephens, Graham Hoskin Les Shakespeare and Terry Middleton all won there games for the home side.

Bugle have moved up to 2nd after a great 4 1 win at struggling Bethel C. Ben Stunell had a great win over Jake Moore to take the solitary home point as Roy Bayliss, Keith Moore and Dave and Colin Rundle all won with 3 frames going to the pink or black ball finish.

