  ('Bethel A stay top of the Victory League', 'bethel-a-stay-top-of-the-victory-league', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Gorran Haven beat Rees league leaders 4-1 at home for a great win with Lee McKinstry having a 38 break', 'Bethel A stay top of the Victory league after a close 3-2 win at home to Luxulyan with Garry Stephens knocking in a first frame 34 break to get them off to a good start with Paul Baron and Matt Green also winning with Ryan Bilson and Gary Spencer replying.', 'Gorran Haven beat Rees league leaders 4-1 at home for a great win with Lee McKinstry having a 38 break', 'Richard Broad, Paul Woodman and Jamie Daniell put Pelynt 3 up at home to Tregonissey A who managed to take the final 2 frames through Jason Cocks and Kevin Harris.

Darren Powell was Mevagissey A s only winner as they lost at home to St Neot who remain in 4th place with Darren Lock, Steve Courts, Ant Maddams and Chris Perring all successful.

Liam Jones beat George Taylor to put Bethel D ahead at St Blazey B but Gavin Dyche knocked in a 53 break to level things up and the home side took the final 3 frames for a good win.

Bethel D played Mevagissey B in a rearranged game the following night and got all 5 frames to lift them off the bottom of the table and leave there unlucky opponents rooted at the base.

Gorran Haven beat Rees league leaders 4-1 at home for a great win with Lee McKinstry having a 38 break as he beat Chris Brown with Mark Cockayne the visitors only success.

Darren Roberts, Jowan Truman and Ryan Orchard all won as Tregonissey B beat Mevagissey C by the odd frame.

Bugle made ground on the leaders beating Tregonissey C by 4 frames to 1 with Predator Tregale taking out Dave Rundle for the single away point.

James Stephens and Les Shakespeare put Lerryn 2 up at Bethel C who managed to win the final 3 frames through Leigh Rosevear, James Smithson and Howard Brett for a welcome victory.

