  ('Team handicap games bring tight matches', 'team-handicap-games-bring-tight-matches', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'St Blazey A picked up a great 3-0 at Pelynt to reach the semi finals with wins for Liam Reynolds,Billy Vigus and Stuart Dewings.', 'Both the Team handicap and Plate competition had a lot of very tight games with plenty of black ball frames.', 'Jason Cocks knocked in a great 64 break whilst defeating Paul Baron', 'Geoff Merriman put Tregonissey A ahead at home to Bethel A beating Garry Stephens but Andy Peers and Matt Green put the visitors ahead only for Jason Cocks to knock in a 64 break whilst defeating Paul Baron leaving Mark Ashton to defeat Andrew Gooch on the pink to settle the game.

St Blazey A picked up a great 3-0 at Pelynt to reach the semi finals with wins for Liam Reynolds,Billy Vigus and Stuart Dewings.

Matt Rowe beat Darren Roberts to put Mevagissey B ahead at Tregonissey B but James Holmes and Ryan Orchard took the next two frames for the home side leaving Jowan Trumans black ball win over Ben Rothwell to seal the win for the treggy boys.

Topsy turvy night at St Neot as Darren Oshea put the home side ahead against St Blazey B with Gavin Dyche levelling up beating Darren Lock on the pink then George Taylor cleared the last 3 balls to defeat Steve Courts putting the visitors ahead but Chris Perrings pink ball defeat of Clive Stuthridge followed by Ant Maddams hammering of Josh Bristow saw the home side progress.

In the Plate competition Colin Rundle, Roy Bayliss and Jake Moore all won on the Black to defeat unlucky Lerryn to send Bugle through.

Mevagissey C had a terrific 3-1 win at Luxulyan with wins for Oliver Watson, Adrian Evans and Mark Ferguson all taking advantage of there handicap starts.

Leigh Rosevear put Bethel C ahead against there D team but spurred on by the Eden projects staff disco karaoke blazing out Jason Pascoe beat Ben Stunell on the Black and wins for Geoff Hawken and Dave Patton saw the D team home.

