  ('Great win for Tregonissey A', 'great-win-for-tregonissey-a', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Lerryn got a fine 4-1 win at home to Tregonissey C to climb the table.', 'Tregonissey A go joint top of the Victory league after a great 4 1 win at Luxulyan Jason Cocks beat Andrew Best in the opener with Gary Spencer levelling things up when beating Geoff Merriman but good wins for Kevin Harris Mark Poulson and Andrew Gooch sees the treggy boys level with Bethel A whose game was postponed.', 'Lerryn got a fine 4-1 win at home to Tregonissey C to climb the table.', 'St Blazey B took 3 points at home to St Neot to rise to 4th in the table Steve Courts and Darren Lock secured the away wins with Gavin Dyche, Josh Bristow and Clive Stuthridge claiming the hosts frames.

Bad night for Bethel D as they only picked up 1 point at home to Mevagissey A through Jason Pascoe with there opponents thoroughly deserving the win with Ben Prynn Matt Chesterfield,Charlie Prynn and Matt Mills all winning.

Bethel B took the first 2 frames at home to Gorran Haven with Mike Haley beating Lee McKinstry and Darren Biggens black ball defeat of Steve Williams but the visitors turned it around with wins for Matt Fox who potted a fantastic pink ball to beat Craig Nicholls and Rob Bunney and Dan Pascoe to keep them very much in the promotion picture.

Lerryn got a fine 4-1 win at home to Tregonissey C to climb the table. Mark Richards got the visitors off to a good start beating Terry Middleton but comfortable wins for John Hancock, David Vipond, Les Shakespeare and James Stephens got the home side there 3rd win of the season.

Bugle rise to 2nd in the table after a terrific 4-1 win at Tregonissey B. Darren Roberts black ball win over Colin Rundle was the only home success with Roy Bayliss Jake Moore Dave Rundle and Keith Moore taking the away honours.

