  ('Gordon Boynton Trophy - Recap', 'gordon-boynton-trophy-recap-3', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, '27 players made the early 10am start at Bethel social club to compete in the Boynton Trophy with the normal 1 frame shootout played off people''s handicap', '26 players took to the green baize on Saturday 28th March to play in the 13th Boynton trophy in honour of the late secretary Gordon at Bethel social club starting at the usual 10 AM start.', null, 'As normal some big names were knocked out early and as the day wound on the semi finals saw Jamie Daniell beat Mark Ashton and Andrew Best get the better of Jason Pascoe to set up a great final with many players still in attendance.

The final was a tight affair which swung around when Andrew potted the blue the white ball went in off leaving Jamie to pot a great blue off its spot and calmly stroked the pink in to clinch the title.

In the Seniors final played at Mevagissey newcomer Ian Millward lifted the trophy as he beat Chris Perring by 3 frames to 0.

Victory League champions Bethel A were beaten 3-2 by the Rest of the league team whilst Rees league champions St Blazey A won 4-1 when they played the Rest of the league.

Mevagissey A beat there C team by 3 frames to 1 in the Team Plate handicap final played at St Blazey and the next night St Neot beat Bethel A in the final of the Team handicap final with wins for Darren Lock Darren Oshea and Steve Courts.', '2026-04-07', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
