  ('Annual General Meeting 2026 (AGM)', 'annual-general-meeting-2026-agm', 'League Meetings', '[]'::jsonb, 'St Blazey and District Snooker League AGM held at Bethel Social Club on Tuesday 21st July 2026 with a 19.30hrs start', 'St Blazey and District Snooker League AGM held at Bethel Social Club on Tuesday 21st July 2026 with a 19.30hrs start', null, 'Present: Chris Perring - President, Garry Stephens - Chairman, Keith Moore - Vice Chairman, Geoff Hawken - Secretary, Ryan Orchard, Clive Stuthridge, Darren Biggen, Matt Green, Gary Spencer, Justin Oxenham all committee. Apologies: Richard Pearson, Lee McInstry.

Chairman garry stephens opened the meeting and thanked everyone for there attendance and immediately thanked our 3 sponsors who had agreed to do another 3 years sponsorship.

He congratulated all the competition and league winners and welcomed Steve Vicary from Luxulyan b who had joined the league for next season.

1. Secretary''s report he thanked everyone who had made the season run so well with special thanks to John Daniell, Rich Pearson and to Mark Cockayne who had done so much work in making the leagues run smoothly sadly Mark is stepping away to have a snooker break so Josh Bristow will be co-opted on to the committee to run the competitions and Clive Stuthridge would oversee any problems on match nights. A meeting between Rich, Clive, Josh, Garry and Geoff would be arranged shortly.
2. Victory League beat Liskeard league by a blue ball shootout in the interleague match after drawing 7 each.
3. Rees league lost 11-3 against the liskeard league division 1 side.
4. A new Interleague match against the mining league would be played at the end of October to play for the Jonathan barron trophy which was last played for in the 1990s the trophy has turned up after many years and both leagues are delighted to start this up again.
5. The Runabout Shield for the Rees Lague would start at Tregonissey C next season after a draw was made.
6. Presentation night was a great success with great camaraderie in the room from players of both leagues the raffle was excellently supported and lots of people stayed on for the band.
7. New season starts on Tuesday 22th September and secretary would get all fixtures/handicaps/rules sheets as soon as they are available.

1. Treasurer report the league had a very good season with a surplus of £730.40 even after purchasing 2 years website hosting accounts were unanimously accepted

1. Rule 21 a team can play with 4 players 5 times a season but the extra player can only play once a season and will be drawn out last on the scorecard when playing the extra game
2. Rule 12 if 2 teams are level for relegation from the victory league or promotion from the rees league the team with the most wins stays or is promoted to the victory if still level the seasons head to head results will be taken into account if still level a playoff match to take place
3. Rule 25 all tables to be ready to play by 19.15hrs and play to start ASAP
4. Team pairs competition a team can use all 5 players over the 4 frames scorecard example 1 + 2 1 + 2 3 + 4 3 + 4 1 + 2 3 + 5 3 + 4 1 + 2

1. After a very long discussion regarding slow play the secretary was asked to email all captions to remind there players not to take unnecessary amounts of time on the shots.
2. A suggestion by Justin oxenham to give £50 prize money to the winner of the bill tom''s and willie Thomas competitions with £25 to the runners up was passed unanimously .

There being no further business the chairman closed the meeting at 20 20.00hrs', '2026-08-04', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
