  ('Luxulyan B-rilliant: Rees League Newcomers Clean Up in Five-Frame Masterclass', 'luxulyan-b-rilliant-rees-league-newcomers-clean-up-in-five-frame-masterclass', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Rees league newcomers Luxulyan B won all 5 frames at home to Tregonissey B', 'In the first week of the new season defending champions Bethel A went 3 up at Mevagissey A but were pegged back as Ben Prynn beat Andy Peers and Matt Mills getting the better of Mark Ashton despite a 34 break from Mark who failed to reach the Black ball to lose the frame.', 'Rees league newcomers Luxulyan B won all 5 frames at home to Tregonissey B', 'Tregonissey A got a good win at home to Luxulyan A with wins for Mark Poulson, Andrew Gooch and Jason Cocks with Justin Oxenham and Gary Spencer replying. Mevagissey B got 4 frames at Bugle with wins for Nathan Shaw, Pete Chambers and 2 wins for Ben Rothwell who didn''t win a frame in the whole 1st half of last season. Pelynt went 3 up at home to St Neot through Phil Ormond, Paul Woodman and Rich Broad but there opponents battled back to take the final 2 frames by Darren Lock and Steve Courts. The B team won the St Blazey Derby by 4 frames to 1 with Darren Roberts the only Victor for the home team beating Ryan Orchard. Rees league newcomers Luxulyan B won all 5 frames at home to Tregonissey B through messes Johnson Remphry, Spencer Vicary and Bennetts to make a great start to the season. Terry Middleton was Lerryns only success as they lost at Gorran Haven with big wins for James Towsey, Lee McKinstry Steve Williams and Matt Fox. Roy Bayliss had a walkover in the final frame to help Bethel B to Victory over Mevagissey C with Adrian Evans and Rich Tamblin getting the away points with Matt Moore and Darren Biggen for the home side. League Sponsor James Smithson beat Geoff Hawken to gain Bethel C’s only frame against there D team who will be looking for a swift return to the Victory league.

