  ('Moore Power as Bugle Edge Past St Neot in Five-Frame Thriller', 'moore-power-as-bugle-edge-past-st-neot-in-five-frame-thriller', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Rees league newcomers Luxulyan B won all 5 frames at home to Tregonissey B', 'Bugle pulled off a great 3-2 win at St Neot with Jake Moore knocking in a 32 break whilst defeating Steve Courts with Keith Moore and Ian Ball also winning with Mark Nicolas and Darren Lock replying.', 'Howard Brett took the prized scalp of Lee McKinstry', 'Phil Ormond potted blue pink and black to beat Mark Ashton getting Pelynts sole point at Bethel A.

There were close frames at St Blazey B as they beat Mevagissey A 3-2 with Ian Millward having a 33 break helping him to victory over Ben Prynn with Ryan Orchard and Josh Bristow also successful for the home side.

St Blazey A picked up 2 useful points at Luxulyan as George Taylor and Martin Richards won with Gary Spencer, Harrison Burdon and Andrew Best notching the hosts frames.

Dave Kendall was Mevagissey B''s only success at home to Tregonissey A as Jason Cocks, Mark Poulson, Geoff Merriman and Andrew Gooch got the away points.

Bethel D beat Tregonissey B 4-1 which was harsh on the treggy boys as all the frames went to the wire with Ryan Taylor playing superly to defeat Steve Benallack for there solitary win.

New boys Luxulyan B went 2 up at Mevagissey C through Kyle Bennetts and Chris Austin but Adrian Evans, Richard Tamblin and Oliver Watson grabbed the final 3 frames to get the home win.

Howard Brett took the prized scalp of Lee McKinstry helping Bethel C beat Gorran by the odd frame with Paul Smithson and Leigh Rosevear also winning with James Towsey and Matt Fox replying.

Bethel Bs good start continued as they went to Tregonissey C and won 4 1 through Craig and Terry Nicholls, Roy Bayliss and Darren Biggen with Mark Richards defeating Matt Moore for the home sides solitary point.

