  ('Cocks and Baron Blaze the Trail as Tregonissey A and Luxulyan B Take League Tops', 'cocks-and-baron-blaze-the-trail-as-tregonissey-a-and-luxulyan-b-take-league-tops', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Tregonissey A beat St Neot by 4 frames to 1 to top the Victory league with Jason Cocks knocking in a 48 break against Steve Courts.', 'Tregonissey A beat St Neot by 4 frames to 1 to top the Victory league with Jason Cocks knocking in a 48 break against Steve Courts to start the ball rolling with wins also for Kevin Harris Geoff Merriman and Andrew Gooch.', 'Tregonissey B found form at Gorran Haven taking 4 frames', 'Bethel A picked up an odd frame win at Bugle to be in 2nd place with Paul Baron having a 45 clearance when beating Dave Rundle in the opening frame with Mark Ashton and Garry Stephens also victorious.

Mevagissey B continued there good start as Ben Rothwell despite a 31 from Chris Brown, Mark Gregory Nathan Shaw and Matt Rowe all won at St Blazey A with Stuart Dewings replying.

Pelynt had a great 4-1 win at home to St Blazey B with Jamie Daniell having a 34 break when beating Ian Millward with Paul Woodman, Phil Ormond and Len Flower also winners in the last frame Josh Bristow had a 30 when beating Richard Broad for the away sides solitary point.

Luxulyan B top the Rees league after getting all 5 frames at home to Tregonissey C with Kyle Bennetts, Simon Johnson, Steve Vicary, Keith Remphry and Kevin Spencer all winning which was harsh on the away side as they were some close frames.

Tregonissey B found form at Gorran Haven taking 4 frames. Matt Fox got the home team of to a good start beating Jowan Truman, but wins for Nate Taylor, Chris Witcombe, Ryan Taylors black ball win over Rob Bunney plus Mark Luczynski win sealed there first win of the season.

Finally Bethel B beat Lerryn by the odd frame thus keeping there hands on the Runabout shield Les Shakespeare and James Stephens took the away points with Roy Bayliss, Craig Nicholls and Darren Biggen successful for the home side.

