  ('Baron''s Break Propels Bethel A as Tregonissey A Defend the Summit', 'barons-break-propels-bethel-a-as-tregonissey-a-defend-the-summit', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Paul Barons fine 42 break and subsequent win over Ben Rothwell means he jumped to the top of the Victory league rankings helping Bethel A to a 4-1 win against Mevagissey B whose only success was Matt Rowe over Andy…', 'Paul Barons fine 42 break and subsequent win over Ben Rothwell means he jumped to the top of the Victory league rankings helping Bethel A to a 4-1 win against Mevagissey B whose only success was Matt Rowe over Andy Peers.', 'St Blazey B got a great win at home to St Neot with Darren Lock stopping the whitewash', 'Tregonissey A stay top after getting 4 frames at home to St Blazey A with 3 games going to the Black ball with Darren Roberts defeating Kev Harris for the away point.

Mevagissey A took 3 frames at home to Bugle with Ben Prynn losing to Jake Moore in the 1st frame of the night but beating him in the last frame as both played the extra player role.

Jamie Daniell and Phil Ormond got Pelynts points at home to luxulyan A with Gary Spencer (34 break) Justin Oxenham and Andrew Best successful for the visitors.

St Blazey B got a great win at home to St Neot with Darren Lock stopping the whitewash beating Josh Bristow with Ian Millward getting the prized scalp of Steve Courts.

Luxulyan B stay top of the Rees league after beating Lerryn 3-2 wins for Steve Vicary, Kevin Spencer and Simon Johnson got them home with James Stephens and Terry Middleton replying.

The Bethel derby went the way of the D team as Geoff Hawken, Liam Jones and Bob Stephens (32 break) all won with Matt Moore and Mark Haworth getting the home points.

In the Tregonissey Derby the B team overcame there C team by the odd frame with victories for Nate Taylor, Chris Witcombe and Jowan Truman with Mark Richards and Darren Elliott replying.

